'' A MACRO IN AN ARGUMENT LIST IS EXPANDED WHILE THE LIST IS READ, so the commas and
'' parentheses it produces separate and nest like written ones. fbc's hLoadMacro lexes
'' an invocation with define-loading on; PpReadArgs split the RAW tokens, so every
'' line below was TKO0306. Found in a user program that sorts with
''
''     #define down >,<
''     SetQsort( V3, QsortvZ, down, .z )     '' a five-parameter #macro
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 on tests/pp/src/macro-arg-expand.bas -- run, then -pp:
''
''     false          true           3             3             2             2
''
''     dim as boolean r1 = (3 > 4), r2 = (3 < 4)
''     dim as long f1 = 1+2
''     dim as long f2 = ( 1)+2
''     dim as long f3 = 2
''     dim as long f4 = 2
''
'' The golden holds those same constants: 3 > 4 and 3 < 4 for r1 and r2, 1 + 2 twice,
'' then 2 and 2 -- the builtins read their arguments the same way.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/pp/src/macro-arg-expand.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/macro-arg-expand.out
